---
import ToolPage from '../../../layouts/ToolPage.astro';

const steps = [
  'Paste HTML into the box, for example a template, a snippet from a UI kit, or something you copied from a website. Or start from the example that’s already there.',
  'Check the preview to see it’s the right piece. The JSX appears next to it right away, with every fix listed on top: <code>class</code> to <code>className</code>, styles to objects, tags closed, comments and SVG attributes fixed.',
  'Copy the JSX, or copy the prompt and paste it into Claude Code, Cursor or Codex so your agent adds it to your project as a component.',
];

const faq = [
  { q: 'Is my HTML sent anywhere?', a: 'No. The conversion runs in your browser. Your HTML never leaves your computer.' },
  { q: 'Why can’t I paste HTML straight into React?', a: 'JSX looks like HTML but has different rules. <code>class</code> is a reserved word in JavaScript so it’s <code>className</code>, <code>style</code> takes an object instead of text, every tag must be closed (<code>&lt;br /&gt;</code>), comments are written <code>{/* like this */}</code>, and SVG attributes like <code>stroke-width</code> become <code>strokeWidth</code>. This tool does all of that for you.' },
  { q: 'What does “Wrap in a component” do?', a: 'It puts the JSX inside <code>export default function YourName() { return (…) }</code>, so you can save it as a file like <code>YourName.jsx</code> or <code>YourName.tsx</code> and use it as <code>&lt;YourName /&gt;</code>. Untick it to get only the JSX.' },
  { q: 'What does “Inline styles to Tailwind” do?', a: 'If your project uses Tailwind, it moves inline styles into Tailwind classes when there’s a class that means the same thing, like <code>display: flex</code> to <code>flex</code> or <code>padding: 16px</code> to <code>p-4</code>. Anything without an exact class stays in <code>style</code>, so nothing changes how it looks.' },
  { q: 'Why did value become defaultValue?', a: 'In React, an input with <code>value</code> can’t be typed into unless you also handle changes. <code>defaultValue</code> (and <code>defaultChecked</code> for checkboxes) keeps the field working like it did in plain HTML.' },
  { q: 'What happens to scripts and onclick?', a: 'Scripts don’t run when React renders them, and inline <code>onclick="…"</code> code becomes an arrow function like <code>onClick={() =&gt; { … }}</code>. The tool warns you when it sees either, so you or your agent can move that code into the component.' },
  { q: 'The preview looks plain. Is something wrong?', a: 'The preview shows your HTML with its inline styles and <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> tags. Classes from Tailwind, Bootstrap or your own CSS files won’t show here because those files aren’t loaded, but the JSX keeps every class.' },
];
---
<ToolPage
  slug="html-to-jsx"
  title="HTML to JSX converter for React (free, private) · Darnly"
  description="Paste HTML and get JSX for React: class to className, styles to objects, tags closed, SVG fixed, with a live preview. Optional Tailwind and component wrapper."
  h1="HTML to JSX: paste HTML, get React code"
  lede="Paste any HTML and get JSX you can drop into a React component, with a live preview so you know you copied the right piece. It runs in your browser, so nothing is uploaded."
  steps={steps}
  faq={faq}
>
  <div class="hj">
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="side">
        <div class="pane-head">
          <span class="lab">What it looks like</span>
          <span class="hint">Live preview</span>
        </div>
        <div class="preview" id="hj-preview" aria-label="Preview of your HTML"></div>

        <div class="pane-head">
          <label for="hj-input" class="lab">Your HTML</label>
          <div class="head-btns">
            <button id="hj-example" type="button" class="ghost">Example</button>
            <button id="hj-clear" type="button" class="ghost">Clear</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <textarea id="hj-input" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" placeholder='<div class="card">Paste HTML here</div>'></textarea>
      </div>

      <div class="side">
        <div class="verdict" id="hj-verdict" aria-live="polite">
          <p class="v-title" id="hj-v-title">Paste HTML to get JSX</p>
          <ul class="chips" id="hj-chips"></ul>
        </div>
        <ul class="warn" id="hj-warn" hidden></ul>

        <div class="code">
          <div class="code-head">
            <span class="code-lab" id="hj-code-lab">JSX</span>
            <button id="hj-copy" type="button" class="copy">Copy JSX</button>
          </div>
          <pre id="hj-code" tabindex="0"></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="options">
          <label class="check"><input id="hj-wrap" type="checkbox" checked /> Wrap in a component</label>
          <label class="name" id="hj-name-wrap">named <input id="hj-name" type="text" maxlength="60" value="SignupCard" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Component name" /></label>
          <label class="check"><input id="hj-tw" type="checkbox" /> Inline styles to Tailwind</label>
        </div>

        <button id="hj-prompt" type="button" class="primary">Copy prompt for your AI agent</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolPage>

<script>
  import '../../../scripts/html-to-jsx';
</script>

<style>
  .hj { min-width: 0; }
  .hj [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; align-items: start; }
  .side { display: grid; gap: 12px; min-width: 0; }
  .pane-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .lab { font-weight: 600; }
  .hint { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .head-btns { display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  .ghost { font: 600 14px/1 var(--body); padding: 9px 14px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; }
  .ghost:hover { border-color: var(--sky); }
  .preview { position: relative; height: 360px; overflow: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: #fff; transform: translateZ(0); contain: paint; }
  textarea { width: 100%; min-height: 260px; font: 400 13px/1.6 var(--mono); font-variant-ligatures: none; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); resize: vertical; tab-size: 2; }
  textarea:focus { outline: 3px solid var(--pink); outline-offset: 1px; }
  .verdict { padding: 16px 18px; border-radius: 16px; background: #E8F7EF; color: #14532D; }
  .verdict.empty { background: var(--wash); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .v-title { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; }
  .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin: 10px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .chips:empty { display: none; }
  .chips :global(li) { font: 500 13px/1 var(--mono); padding: 7px 10px; border-radius: 999px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75); color: #14532D; }
  .warn { margin: 0; padding: 12px 16px 12px 34px; border-radius: 12px; background: #FFF6E0; color: #6B4A00; font-size: 14px; display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .code { border-radius: 16px; background: var(--ink); color: #D9EEF6; overflow: hidden; min-width: 0; }
  .code-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 8px 10px 8px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(217, 238, 246, 0.12); }
  .code-lab { font: 500 13px/1 var(--mono); color: #8FB4C4; }
  .copy { font: 600 13px/1 var(--body); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 8px; border: 0; background: var(--sky); color: var(--white); cursor: pointer; }
  .code pre { margin: 0; padding: 16px; height: 440px; overflow: auto; font: 400 13px/1.7 var(--mono); font-variant-ligatures: none; tab-size: 2; }
  .options { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px 16px; }
  .check { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 15px; }
  .name { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-soft); margin-left: -8px; }
  .name input { width: 150px; font: 400 14px/1.2 var(--mono); padding: 7px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); }
  .name.off { opacity: 0.45; }
  .primary { justify-self: start; font: 600 15px/1 var(--body); padding: 13px 20px; border-radius: 999px; border: 0; background: var(--pink); color: var(--white); cursor: pointer; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .preview { height: 280px; }
    .code pre { height: 360px; }
    textarea { min-height: 200px; }
  }
</style>
